[~accountid:5ad5a3d0af21cf2a74841d6d] please note that, pursuant to § 9.3 “all payments under the lease agreement will be paid in advance by Bolt within 7 days of the start of each consecutive month's rent, unless another payment period has been agreed”. To be confirmed if 7-days payment term is acceptable from the business perspective.

Please also note that the Landlord is autorised to:

* [§ 5.3] open and empty the Box at Bolt's expense in the event that Bolt fails to pay the Rent within 14 days of the date on which payment of the Rent became due.  In such a case, the Landlord will be entitled to take ownership of the items stored in the Box or dispose of them at Bolt's expense;
* [§8.1] terminate the agreement with immediate effect in the event of non-payment of rent by Bolt on the date on which payment of rent became due or failure to comply with the obligations assumed by Bolt in the lease agreement;

If any changes are possible, I would suggest adding to these provisions that the LL is autorised to take these actions upon submission to Bolt of a request setting an additional, no shorter than 7-days deadline.

* [§ 11.2] Charge a contractual penalty in the amount of PLN 20,000 in case the lease agreement is terminated with immediate effect by the Landlord for reasons attributable to Bolt;
* [§ 11.3] Charge interest up to the maximum amount permitted by law in case Bolt is in a one-month delay in rent payment by Bolt.

In addition, pursuant to § 11.6 if payment for the Box rental is not made by the due date, an additional padlock will be applied within one day after the due date and the Access Code will be deactivated. Access to the Box will be reinstated within 3 working days after payment of the arrears. The fee for re-granting access is PLN 100.

Hi [~accountid:6270f0bd807e0000691b79bb] !

{quote}*Is there any situation currently where we can skip consent or do you still need to assess this?*{quote}

We need to assess this, we cannot move forward without consent at this stage - where we use live location tracking. As said, we can try to re-assess in Q1 - but I think more likely consent will be needed.

For cases where we do not use live location tracking, please clearly map them out and likely we will be able to proceed without consent. *Q: what is the main factor to categorise offers as “Travelling” atm for LCM Rides? Is this live-location tracking?* 

{quote}the way we promote opting into consents is by modals and banners in the Rider app - should we include a disclaimer in these in-apps? Or should we add the disclaimers directly in the communication preferences in the app?{quote}

We need to inform users in the modals where we ask for consent. We can collaborate and privacy can give you input on exactly how consent is obtained.

{quote}#  what about already collected consents that didn’t have this disclaimer? Can we consider those users consented to being targeted with live location data as well or do we need to retroactively update them some other way?{quote}

Depends on how we worded the consent when we originally obtained it and if the wording could cover the updated processing. I understand both cases we would have to inform about live data tracking for marketing - wouldn’t` we? Please share with the privacy team the original wording and clarification from your side how much change occurred so we can assess.

{quote}Existing consent-collecting in-apps can be found [+*here*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10eNnvT2mJt2wTm6ZgNO70vSEv9wFkdVWNn9_mm2pDVM/edit?gid=0#gid=0]+*.*+ Rider app screen is attached below - considering it’s specifically mentioning “receive local transportation suggestions based on your location *when abroad*”, do we need to change this as well? Could you help suggest a better wording for this to cover all the cases we want to implement?{quote}

Yes, we can - I understand this can be done in Q1. Please confirm.

{quote}* In-apps - do I understand correctly that even for comms that don’t use live location we will still need to implement consent to promote travel content via in-apps? Or alternatively, wait for you to reassess whether we can skip consent for all channels.{quote}

No. Travel content can be promoted without consent (as long as it does not promote specific their parties) as long as we do not use live data.

{quote}Given that in Q1 we’d like to start using the polygon functionality in Admin which requires us to target users based on their live location, would the *end of January* be a reasonable deadline for your team to reassess the above and provide us with the necessary conclusions around live-location data? This way, we can already start working on any needed changes in February.{quote}

Yes, I think so. Have you considered submitting this as an MVRA project for Rides for Q1?

