{quote}_For cases where we do not use live location tracking, please clearly map them out and likely we will be able to proceed without consent._ *_Q: what is the main factor to categorise offers as “Travelling” atm for LCM Rides? Is this live-location tracking?_*{quote}

Not all travelling comms involve live-location tracking. *Example:* return airport trip comms - we want to be able to nudge riders to schedule their next airport ride in advance once they have completed 1 airport trip recently. The idea here is to ensure we can capture the "return" leg of a rider’s/tourist's journey while providing them a reliable option in terms of scheduling trip in advance. This particular example will not rely on live-location, but instead on historical location data, e.g. he recently did an airport trip, he might need a return trip. We can map out other use-cases as well, but was wondering if in cases such as this one consent is needed or not. 



{quote}_We need to inform users in the modals where we ask for consent. We can collaborate and privacy can give you input on exactly how consent is obtained._{quote}

As an alternative, considering the space is quite limited in our in-apps and they don’t automatically opt users in, but instead redirect to the communication preferences in the app, could we not add the information in that screen instead? The user still needs to manually toggle the consents on, so he can read all the information beforehand, in the same screen. This needs to be aligned with Rider X as well, but just want to confirm with you first. I will also raise it with them to confirm if possible to amend this screen in Q1, but would need to have the wording ready.



{quote}_Please share with the privacy team the original wording and clarification from your side how much change occurred so we can assess._{quote}

Shared the wording in my previous message - in-apps content is [+*here*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10eNnvT2mJt2wTm6ZgNO70vSEv9wFkdVWNn9_mm2pDVM/edit?gid=0#gid=0], while the travelling consent screen in the app is shared above. To my knowledge, this hasn’t changed since it was implemented. 



{quote}No. Travel content can be promoted without consent (as long as it does not promote specific their parties) as long as we do not use live data.{quote}

Not sure I understood this part completely. Also, what about the use-case shared above, where we don’t use live location data, but historical? Can we consider it a hard rule that if we don’t need live location data, then we can promote travel content without consent?



{quote}Yes, I think so. Have you considered submitting this as an MVRA project for Rides for Q1?{quote}

The first use-case we want to test is based on the polygons functionality which already exists and is currently being used by the Growth team. For this specific case, we only have a dependency on Growth exclusively. But for future cases, we will need to involve Product as well, yes.

Btw, I will be in Tallinn office between Dec 17-19, it would maybe be easier to discuss face to face as well, if you’re available. 🙂

